# Keep the CI image a tree, not a history.
#
# .git is excluded so nothing inside the container can read or write repository history, and so the
# image content is exactly the files under test. scripts/ci-stages.mjs takes the commit SHA from the
# CI_COMMIT_SHA environment variable instead, which the host script sets from the SHA it verified.
.git

# .gitignore is deliberately NOT excluded: test/local-ci.test.mjs asserts that artifacts/local-ci is
# unignorable-by-accident, and a check that cannot see the file it checks would skip silently.

# Transient verification output. Bind-mounted in at run time by scripts/ci.* so results reach the
# host; baking a previous run's result into the image would let a stale pass be reported as current.
artifacts/local-ci

# Never present in this repository (zero dependencies), listed so a reused copy of this file does not
# silently ship a host-built node_modules into the image.
node_modules

*.log
.DS_Store
Dockerfile.ci
compose.ci.yml
